To apply the exact same smooth "Read More" animation and professional layout to your VoucherBulkUpload.jsx file, you need to make three quick changes.
Here is exactly what to do.
### 1. Add the Missing Imports
At the top of your file, add Collapse to your @mui/material imports, and add the two Arrow icons to your @mui/icons-material imports.
**Update your imports to include these:**
```javascript
import {
  // ... your other imports
  Collapse 
} from "@mui/material";

import {
  // ... your other imports
  KeyboardArrowUpIcon,
  KeyboardArrowDownIcon
} from "@mui/icons-material";

```
### 2. Add the State & Description Logic
Find where you define your state variables (around line 50), and add the state for the description toggle. Then, right before your return statement, calculate if the description is long enough to need a "Read More" button.
**Add this near your other useState hooks:**
```javascript
  const [isDescExpanded, setIsDescExpanded] = useState(false);

```
**Add this right before your return ( statement (around line 300):**
```javascript
  const desc = selectedVoucher?.DESCRIPTION || selectedVoucher?.description || "No description provided.";
  const isLongDesc = desc.length > 100 || desc.split(/\r?\n/).length > 2;

```
### 3. Replace the Description Grid
Find the Grid item containing the description inside your return statement (around line 344) and replace it with the new animated box.
**FIND THIS:**
```javascript
            <Grid item xs={12}>
              <Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary" display="block" gutterBottom>Description</Typography>
              <Typography variant="body2" sx={jbuStyles.svDescription}>
                {selectedVoucher.DESCRIPTION || selectedVoucher.description || "No description provided."}
              </Typography>
              {/* </Box> */}
            </Grid>

```
**REPLACE WITH THIS:**
```javascript
            <Grid item xs={12}>
              <Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary" display="block" gutterBottom>
                Description
              </Typography>
              
              <Box sx={{ position: "relative" }}>
                {/* collapsedSize={44} perfectly frames about 2 lines of body2 text */}
                <Collapse in={!isLongDesc || isDescExpanded} collapsedSize={44}>
                  <Typography variant="body2" sx={{ whiteSpace: "pre-wrap", lineHeight: 1.6, fontWeight: 400, color: "text.primary" }}>
                    {desc}
                  </Typography>
                </Collapse>
                
                {isLongDesc && (
                  <Box sx={{ display: "flex", justifyContent: "flex-start", mt: 0.5 }}>
                    <Button
                      size="small"
                      disableRipple
                      onClick={() => setIsDescExpanded(!isDescExpanded)}
                      endIcon={isDescExpanded ? <KeyboardArrowUpIcon /> : <KeyboardArrowDownIcon />}
                      sx={{
                        p: 0,
                        minWidth: "auto",
                        textTransform: "none",
                        fontWeight: 600,
                        color: "primary.main",
                        "&:hover": { background: "transparent", textDecoration: "underline" }
                      }}
                    >
                      {isDescExpanded ? "Read Less" : "Read More"}
                    </Button>
                  </Box>
                )}
              </Box>
            </Grid>

```
This perfectly mirrors the design from your manual entry screen, ensuring a consistent, polished look across both upload methods!
